<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Nop.Web.MVC.Tests - migrated by task 17.1 (Requirements 5.6, 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 4.2, 5.3, 3.1).

    This is the last of the five test projects and the last leaf task before the solution-file
    group (18). Converted from the classic (non-SDK) MSBuild format following the pattern of the
    already-migrated test projects - src/Tests/Nop.Tests (task 4.5) is the closest analogue, with
    src/Tests/Nop.Admin.Tests and src/Tests/Nop.Web.SmokeTests as the other SDK-style test
    projects modelled on.

    DROPPED IN THE CONVERSION
    =========================
      * ToolsVersion / DefaultTargets / xmlns MSBuild-2003 attributes; ProjectGuid
        {57718244-1B22-4637-9DBF-F5D8E460FC95}, ProductVersion, SchemaVersion, FileAlignment,
        AppDesignerFolder, TargetFrameworkProfile, NuGetPackageImportStamp; OutputType (Library
        is the SDK default); RootNamespace/AssemblyName (both already equal the project name).
      * TargetFrameworkVersion v4.5.1 and the Debug|AnyCPU / Release|AnyCPU PropertyGroup pair
        (Prefer32Bit, WarningLevel, DefineConstants, etc.) - the SDK supplies equivalents.
      * The explicit <Compile Include="..."/> list of 35 files - replaced by SDK implicit globbing
        (which now globs 32 files: the three Public/Infrastructure/Routes* files were removed, see
        the ROUTING note below).
      * Every MVC-5 / System.Web <Reference>: System.Web, System.Web.Mvc, System.Web.Razor,
        System.Web.Helpers, System.Web.WebPages(.Deployment/.Razor), and the BCL
        <Reference Include="System.*"/> entries (System, System.Core, System.Net,
        System.Net.Http(.WebRequest), System.Xml(.Linq), System.Data(.DataSetExtensions),
        Microsoft.CSharp) - subsumed by the net10.0 shared framework / no longer referenced.
      * The Microsoft.Bcl / Microsoft.Bcl.Async / Microsoft.Net.Http / Microsoft.Web.Infrastructure
        <Reference> + HintPath entries and the Microsoft.Bcl.Build .targets Import plus its
        EnsureNuGetPackageBuildImports target - all net45-era polyfills that net10.0 does not need.
      * WebActivator - a System.Web (PreApplicationStartMethod) package with no ASP.NET Core
        counterpart. VERIFIED unused: no [assembly: PreApplicationStartMethod], no
        WebActivator(Ex) attribute, and no `using WebActivator*` anywhere in this project. Dropped,
        not replaced.
      * <None Include="App.config"/> + <None Include="packages.config"/> and the three
        <Content Include="*/Readme.txt"/> placeholder-doc items. packages.config and App.config are
        deleted (Requirements 1.3, 1.5). App.config carried only a NopConfig configSection stub and
        a wall of net45 binding redirects (System.Web.Mvc, WebGrease, Antlr3, MiniProfiler, OWIN,
        OData, Redis-StrongName ...) - every one of those assemblies is gone from the migrated
        graph, so there is nothing to redirect.

    KEPT
    ====
      * Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs - matching Nop.Core / Nop.Data / Nop.Services / Nop.Web and the
        other converted projects. GenerateAssemblyInfo=false is set solution-wide in
        src/Directory.Build.props (task 2.3), so the SDK emits NO replacement attributes; removing
        this file would drop AssemblyVersion from 3.9.0.0 to 0.0.0.0 (measured on Nop.Web at tasks
        7.5/8.1). It stays authoritative.

    ROUTING TESTS - DROPPED, COVERAGE MOVED (faithfulness note; recorded in runtime-deferrals.md 17.1)
    ================================================================================================
      Public/Infrastructure/RoutesTests.cs, RoutesTestsBase.cs and RouteTestingExtensions.cs were
      deleted. They tested MVC-5 URL->route resolution through System.Web.Routing.RouteTable /
      RouteCollection.GetRouteData / HttpContextBase and the ported Nop.Web RouteProvider now
      registers ENDPOINT routes over IEndpointRouteBuilder (task 7.3) with slug routing through
      SlugRouteTransformer - there is no RouteTable to populate and no RouteCollection overload to
      call, so a line-by-line port is not possible. The equivalent coverage - real endpoint routing
      asserted against the running host via EndpointDataSource / RouteEndpoint.RoutePattern and the
      real LinkGenerator - already lives in src/Tests/Nop.Web.SmokeTests (tasks 7.7 / 8.8), so it is
      referenced, not duplicated. See runtime-deferrals.md for exactly what was kept, moved and
      dropped.

    MOCKING - RhinoMocks -> NSubstitute (USER-APPROVED)
    ===================================================
      RhinoMocks 3.6.1 is .NET-Framework-only with no net10.0 build. NSubstitute (pinned centrally
      at 6.2.0, BSD-3-Clause) replaces it in the six files that used it. The rewrites:
        MockRepository.GenerateMock<T>()            -> Substitute.For<T>()
        MockRepository.GeneratePartialMock<T>()     -> Substitute.ForPartsOf<T>()
        .Expect(x => x.M()).Return(v)               -> x.M().Returns(v)  (or Configure().M().Returns(v)
                                                       for a partial, so real code does not run)
        .Expect(...).Return(v).IgnoreArguments()    -> M(Arg.Any<...>()).Returns(v)
      See src/Directory.Packages.props (the Mocking ItemGroup) for the version/license verification.

    TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, GenerateAssemblyInfo and the shared assembly
    metadata come from src/Directory.Build.props; net10.0 is restated so the target framework is
    verifiable from this file (Requirement 1.2).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    packages.config -> PackageReference (Requirements 1.3, 1.5). Versions are governed centrally by
    src/Directory.Packages.props, so every item is intentionally version-less.

      Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk / NUnit / NUnit3TestAdapter - the runnable test-project trio, same as
        Nop.Tests / Nop.Admin.Tests / Nop.Web.SmokeTests. NUnit is pinned 3.14.0 centrally (NUnit 4
        removed the classic Assert.AreEqual/IsInstanceOf surface these tests use).
      NSubstitute - replaces RhinoMocks (see the MOCKING note above).

    AutoMapper and FluentValidation are NOT declared here even though the tests use them: they flow
    transitively through the ProjectReferences (FluentValidation from Nop.Web.Framework via task
    6.1 - the tests use FluentValidation 7.6.105, design section 9; AutoMapper from Nop.Services /
    Nop.Admin). The validator TestHelper types (ShouldHaveValidationErrorFor) live in
    FluentValidation.TestHelper, which is part of the same FluentValidation assembly on 7.x.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit" />
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit3TestAdapter" />
    <PackageReference Include="NSubstitute" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ProjectReferences point at the migrated SDK-style projects (Requirement 2.4). The legacy
    <Project>{guid}</Project> / <Name> metadata children are dropped - the SDK resolves by path.

    Nop.Admin is the nested src/Presentation/Nop.Web/Administration/Nop.Admin.csproj; a
    ProjectReference to it makes MSBuild build it first (it is at 0 errors). Nop.Web is referenced
    for its controllers/models/validators (AddressValidator, RegisterValidator, the storefront
    models); Nop.Admin for AdminMapperConfiguration and the admin validators; Nop.Web.Framework for
    AdminAuthorizeAttribute and the CreditCard validator; Nop.Tests for TestsBase / the Should*
    assertion extensions; Nop.Core / Nop.Services / Nop.Data are the libraries the tests bind
    directly (NopEngine, NopConfig, IConsumer, ILocalizationService, IStateProvinceService,
    IInstallationLocalizationService).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Data\Nop.Data.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Services\Nop.Services.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web.Framework\Nop.Web.Framework.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Administration\Nop.Admin.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Nop.Web.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Nop.Tests\Nop.Tests.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
